---
to: "src/gymact_consumer_mcp_tools.rs"
sparql:
  ops: |
    PREFIX dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>
    PREFIX sosa: <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/>
    SELECT ?id ?consequence_class
    WHERE {
      ?cap a sosa:Procedure ;
           dct:title ?id ;
           dct:type ?consequence_class_iri .
      BIND(IF(CONTAINS(STR(?consequence_class_iri), "consequence:do"), "Do", "Read") AS ?consequence_class)
    }
    ORDER BY ?id
---
//! Generated MCP tool schema surface -- GENERATED by `ggen sync` from
//! this pack's own `ontology.ttl` (YOUR capability facts, not GymAct's
//! built-in operations). Tool NAME PREFIX below is `consumer.` as a
//! placeholder -- replace it with your own system's slug (e.g.
//! `autofde.`) before syncing for real, so generated tool names don't
//! collide with GymAct's own `gymact.*` MCP surface
//! (`~/gymact/src/gymact/surfaces/fastmcp.py`) if both are ever loaded
//! into the same MCP client.
//!
//! `consequence_class` is surfaced as a schema field, not enforced here:
//! per GymAct's architecture, an MCP tool call manufactures an intent, it
//! never grants execution authority by itself. Authority itself remains
//! Python-runtime-only in GymAct today (an injected `AuthorityResolver`,
//! see `~/gymact/.claude/rules/actuation-authority.md`), not represented
//! in RDF -- do not invent an RDF authority vocabulary here to work
